  The proof is divided into thirty-two units grouped by mathematical subject
  in eight parts. Each page contains its outline, pinned Lean references and
  selected statements. Allocation of declarations to a unit is distinct from
  the mathematical inputs needed to understand its argument; see the
  <hlink|overview|index.tm> and <hlink|data|../data/index.tm>.

  All outlines are available. The status links below explain the three review
  rounds: <hlink|draft|../method.tm#unit-outline-status>,
  <hlink|checked|../method.tm#unit-outline-status> and
  <hlink|edited|../method.tm#unit-outline-status>. A status describes the
  review of the explanation; each unit's \PWhat remains unexplained\Q section
  gives its remaining limits. Source-size figures are collected <hlink|below
  the index|#source-statistics>.

